cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this code or the analyses it implements, please cite it.
title: >-
  Objective allowances and growth assumptions shape transcript-informed exchange predictions
  in a human metabolic model
abstract: >-
  Code, protocol records, derived data and result tables for a controlled study of the interface
  between transcript-derived reaction scores and constraint-based prediction of metabolic
  exchange. Measures how often rank-preserving changes to score spacing alter predicted
  extracellular exchange and its agreement with measurement, attributes the reported exchange
  coordinates to the network, the objectives with their allowances and the transcript costs,
  sweeps the objective allowances, compares a bound-based interface and a published sampling
  workflow under the same evaluation, and tests a unanimity reporting rule on an independent
  condition-response dataset. The repository is laid out as the study root named by its protocol
  lock, so the locked pipeline and the post-lock analyses run from a checkout.
